 "notes": "Boundary of the solid-blue 'ALP SN1987A (excl. 95%)' region in Fig. 1 (e-print Plots/Limits_18p6.pdf), extracted from the vector PDF stroke path with axes calibrated to the plot frame (m_a: 1e-12..1e-1 eV, g_agamma: 1e-16..1e-8 GeV^-1, log-log). This is the paper's headline measured 95% CL upper limit from non-observation of SMM gamma-rays coincident with SN1987A, combining axion-photon conversion in the Galactic magnetic field (weakest Unger-Farrar ensemble model, dominant for m_a < ~1e-9 eV) and in the progenitor (BSG) stellar magnetic field with a conservative surface field B0 = 100 G; fiducial SN simulation SFHo-18.6; ALP scenario with loop-induced (RG) hadronic couplings only. The alternative hatched 'KSVZ-like axion SN1987A' curve (tree-level KSVZ hadronic coupling ratios, stronger limit) is not reported. Calibration validated: the black 'SN1987A (prev. work)' line extracts to 5.23e-12 GeV^-1 at low mass. Note the main text quotes a low-mass limit of 2.6e-12 GeV^-1 while the plotted curve is flat at 3.66e-12 GeV^-1 (~sqrt(2) apart); the plotted Fig. 1 curve is reported. Limit does not assume axion dark matter, so no density rescaling applies.",
